# The project's fields: one stanza per field, separated by a blank line, in
# the order pidly writes them into a new ticket.
#
#   field:     the name, which is the key on its line in a ticket's info
#   required:  yes means a ticket is not valid until the field has a value
#   match:     a POSIX ERE the value must match, tested anchored as ^(...)$
#   note:      one line, for whoever opens this file
#
# Everything after "match: " is the pattern, so | [ ] { } and spaces need no
# escaping. Keep to POSIX ERE: \d, \w, \s, \b and (?...) are PCRE, and
# pidly reports them rather than trusting whichever grep is installed here.
#
# Lines 1, 2 and 3 of a ticket are claim:, needs: and title:. They are the
# format's, not the project's, and are not declared here. Neither are
# created: and updated:, which are pidly's own stamps.

field: effort
match: S|M|L
note: rough size

field: area
match: format|cli|docs
note: which part of the project this is

field: handoff
note: where the last agent got to when they stopped
